    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133">

                <pb facs="0284" n="152" xml:id="pg152"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 E.
                    W./7–945: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 133 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-09T12:00:00+02:00">July 9,
                            1945—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6879. Downing Street has provided us with full list of Brit delegation to
                        meeting.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d133-f1"/> (See your 5409, July 3<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d133-f2"/>).</p>
                <p>
                    Churchill will be accompanied by
                    daughter Mary and personal staff of
                    twelve. Attlee is going. FonOff delegation principals as in our 6566,
                    June 29<anchor n="2" xml:id="d133-f3"/> with addition F. [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] J. G.
                        Ward who has been to several big meetings. Hayter is Secretary General FonOff delegation.</p>
                <p>Other principals are Lord Leathers,
                        Admiral Sir Andrew Cunningham,
                        Field Marshal Sir Alan Brooke,
                    Marshal of RAF
                    Sir Charles Portal, Sir Edward Bridges, Sir Hastings Ismay, Field Marshals Alexander and Wilson, General
                        Gammell, Sir Walter
                        Monckton (Solicitor General)[,] Lord
                        Cherwell (Paymaster General formerly Professor Lindemann) and Colonel Sir Eric Crankshaw (in charge of catering and
                    general hospitality).</p>
                <p>Staff of interpreters is headed by Major A.
                        Birse for PriMin and Major L. M. Theakstone who is Secretary.</p>
                <p>Total Brit delegation will be approximately 250 in number.</p>
                <p>Full list by airmail also to Murphy.</p>
                <p>This telegram plus names of principals of FonOff delegation repeated to Murphy as 26.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
